  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Satellite imagery for this morning\ndepicts mostly clear skies with high clouds streaming across\nnorthern Nevada. Upper level high pressure off the coast of\nCalifornia will continue to build across northern and central\nNevada today bringing mostly sunny skies and afternoon\ntemperatures in the upper 50s to mid 60s. Winds will be on the\nlight side though afternoon breezes to 20 mph are possible across\nnorthern Nevada, north of I-80. Look for another quiet night\ntonight with dry conditions and lows in the 20s and 30s.\n\nHigh pressure is expected to remain in control of northern and\ncentral Nevada's weather through the week. Highs will be in the\n50s and 60s through this time period while overnight lows will be\nin the 20s and 30s. Winds will be on the light side, though wind\ngusts to 20 mph are possible each afternoon from time to time. \n\nBeginning the latter portions of the upcoming weekend, models\ncontinue to hint at the possibility of an upper trough trying to \npush into Nevada. Although still very early, there are a few signs\nof an atmospheric river component with this system that long \nrange models are picking up on. So the possibility of a return of \nrain and snow showers will need to be watched over the several \ndays.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No changes were made to the NBM\ngrids for this forecast period. Confidence remains high in the \nupper level high pressure maintaining control of northern and \ncentral Nevada's weather. Confidence continues to remain low with \nrespect to the upper level trough for the upcoming weekend due to \nstrength and timing differences.",
